                },
                "content": "<div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-xs-12\"><div class=\"learnosity-feature\" data-type=\"scrollablepassage\" data-height=\"100%\"><span class=\"learnosity-response question-_da1afed55a7bfb8aa774df13c30aa8d8\"></span></div></div></div>",
                "metadata": {
                    "rubric_reference": "VH911603_rubric"
                },
                "workflow": [],
                "response_ids": [
                    "_da1afed55a7bfb8aa774df13c30aa8d8"
                ],
                "feature_ids": [],
                "questions": [
                    {
                        "metadata": {
                            "distractor_rationale_response_level": [
                                "<p class=\"rationale_paragraph\" xmlns=\"http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/apip/apipv1p0/qtiitem/imsqti_v2p2\" xmlns:xsi=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\">Correct. Direction is accurate on Mercator projection maps. Mercator maps are used for navigation charts because any straight line on a Mercator projection map is a constant compass bearing along a straight-line course. However, because the actual distance between longitude lines decreases as one moves away from the Equator, objects near the poles are greatly exaggerated in size in the Mercator projection.</p>",
                                "<p class=\"rationale_paragraph\" xmlns=\"http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/apip/apipv1p0/qtiitem/imsqti_v2p2\" xmlns:xsi=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\">Incorrect. The Robinson projection uses a combination of mathematical approaches to represent the three-dimensional globe as a flat map. In doing this, the Robinson projection compromises direction in order to better achieve proportional area. Direction is accurate on Mercator projection maps, but the size of some areas may be exaggerated.</p>",
                                "<p class=\"rationale_paragraph\" xmlns=\"http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/apip/apipv1p0/qtiitem/imsqti_v2p2\" xmlns:xsi=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\">Incorrect. Just as area is distorted on the Mercator Projection, distances are most accurate at the Equator and are increasingly stretched closer to the poles. Direction is accurate on Mercator projection maps, but the size of some areas may be exaggerated.</p>",
                                "<p class=\"rationale_paragraph\" xmlns=\"http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/apip/apipv1p0/qtiitem/imsqti_v2p2\" xmlns:xsi=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\">Incorrect. Although the distortion is spread throughout the entire Robinson projection rather than concentrated in the polar regions, both shape and direction are inaccurate in the Robinson projection. Direction is accurate on Mercator projection maps, but the size of some areas may be exaggerated.</p>",
                                "<p class=\"rationale_paragraph\" xmlns=\"http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/apip/apipv1p0/qtiitem/imsqti_v2p2\" xmlns:xsi=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\">Incorrect. The Mercator projection does not provide accurate size for land areas, especially in the polar regions. Direction is accurate on Mercator projection maps, but the size of some areas may be exaggerated.</p>"
                            ],
                            "valid_response_count": 1,
                            "sheet_reference": "VH911603",
                            "widget_reference": "VH911603_RESPONSE",
                            "source": {
                                "organisation_id": 537
                            }
                        },
                        "stimulus": "<div>\n<div class=\"stimulus_reference\">\n<div class=\"standalone_image\"><img alt=\"The figure presents two maps of the Earth, one labeled Mercator Projection and the other labeled Robinson Projection. The Mercator Projection shows parallel lines of latitude spaced farther and farther apart as distance from the equator increases. The Robinson Projection shows gently curving meridians and flattened north and south poles.\" height=\"255\" src=\"https://assets.learnosity.com/organisations/537/VH911603.g01.png\" width=\"540\" /></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n<p class=\"stem_paragraph\">Which of the following statements is an accurate comparison of the two map projections shown?</p>\n",
                        "type": "mcq",
                        "validation": {
                            "scoring_type": "exactMatch",
                            "valid_response": {
                                "score": 1,
                                "value": [
                                    "i1"
                                ]
                            }
                        },
                        "options": [
                            {
                                "label": "<p class=\"choice_paragraph\">The Mercator projection accurately shows direction but distorts the size of some areas compared to the Robinson projection.</p>",
                                "value": "i1"
                            },
                            {
                                "label": "<p class=\"choice_paragraph\">The Robinson projection accurately shows direction but distorts the size of some areas compared to the Mercator projection.</p>",
                                "value": "i2"
                            },
                            {
                                "label": "<p class=\"choice_paragraph\">The Mercator projection accurately shows distances but distorts direction compared to the Robinson projection.</p>",
                                "value": "i3"
                            },
                            {
                                "label": "<p class=\"choice_paragraph\">The Robinson projection accurately shows shapes but distorts direction compared to the Mercator projection.</p>",
                                "value": "i4"
                            },
                            {
                                "label": "<p class=\"choice_paragraph\">The Mercator projection accurately shows area but distorts shapes compared to the Robinson projection.</p>",
                                "value": "i5"
                            }
                        ],
                        "ui_style": {
                            "type": "horizontal"
                        },
                        "response_id": "_da1afed55a7bfb8aa774df13c30aa8d8"
